<title>USA: MARYLAND $100 MLN DEVELOPMENT BONDS RESTRUCTURED.</title>
<headline>MARYLAND $100 MLN DEVELOPMENT BONDS RESTRUCTURED.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc said Wednesday it restructured Maryland's $100 million Community Development Administration revenue bond deal, adding a 2025 maturity and eliminating a 2026 maturity.</p>
<p>The restructuring follows:</p>
<p>COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT ADMINISTRATION</p>
<p>DEPARTMENT OF HOUSING AND COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT</p>
<p>STATE OF MARYLAND</p>
<p>RE: $100,000,000</p>
<p>RESIDENTIAL REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>1997 SERIES A AND 1997 SERIES B</p>
<p>THIS ISSUE WILL BE IN BOOK ENTRY FORM THROUGH THE FACILITIES</p>
<p>OF DTC</p>
<p>UPDATED STRUCTURE</p>
<p>NOTE THE ADDITION OF 09/01/2025, THE ELIMINATION OF 03/01/2026</p>
<p>AND PAR AMOUNT CHANGES TO RELATED MATURITIES.</p>
